<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="hero-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Reminders</p>
    <h1>Bills, met<br><em>on time.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      Ei Void remembers the payment so you do not have to. Reminders are
      scheduled on the phone, synced as a snapshot, and delivered through the
      channels you choose — Discord, email, or both.
    </p>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download">Get the preview</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/getting-started">Set it up <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">On the phone</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">A ledger that tells the truth.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Amount, merchant, bank, currency, due date and repeat rule. Ei Void
        normalises the entry, schedules the notification and keeps the next
        occurrence ready.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature">
        <p class="feature-index">01</p>
        <h3>Repeat rules</h3>
        <p>One-off, weekly, monthly, quarterly or yearly. The next due date is derived, never retyped.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <p class="feature-index">02</p>
        <h3>Quiet scheduling</h3>
        <p>Pick the hour and minute you want to hear about it. Notifications run on the device first, so a network blip does not lose the reminder.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <p class="feature-index">03</p>
        <h3>Two delivery paths</h3>
        <p>A linked Discord account can receive a DM. Email works when you enable it and sync an address with the app.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <p class="feature-index">04</p>
        <h3>Mark it paid</h3>
        <p>From the app or the bot, a paid reminder leaves the upcoming list. History stays on the phone.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <p class="feature-index">05</p>
        <h3>Your data</h3>
        <p>The website stores the reminder snapshot, not your bank credentials or repository content. Delete the account and the rows cascade.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <p class="feature-index">06</p>
        <h3>One identity</h3>
        <p>Clerk signs you in. The same account links Discord, holds the plan and shows usage in the dashboard.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">The loop</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">From entry to inbox.</h2>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/how') %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <p class="kicker">What leaves the phone</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">A snapshot, not a ledger of everything.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        The app sends reminder fields and delivery preferences to this website
        so the bot and the dashboard can answer. It never sends provider keys,
        bank credentials or repository contents.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Title, amount, due date and repeat rule</li>
        <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Timezone and notification hour</li>
        <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Discord id and username, only after you link</li>
        <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> The address you explicitly enable for email</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="text-link" href="/privacy">Read the privacy page <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="split-visual">
      <div class="boundary-card">
        <div class="boundary-head">
          <span class="boundary-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="mono">reminder sync</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="boundary-code"><code>POST /api/v1/reminders/sync
Authorization: Bearer &lt;Clerk token&gt;

{
  "profile": {
    "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata",
    "notifyHour": 9,
    "emailEnabled": true
  },
  "reminders": [ ... ]
}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="boundary-caption">Parameterised SQL through the shared Store.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head section-head-row">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Plans</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Reminders on every plan.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          The reminder sync is part of the base app. Plans describe token
          budgets for the agent half of Ei Void.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/pricing">Compare plans <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="plans-grid">
      <% plans.forEach(function (plan) { %>
        <%- include('partials/plan', { plan: plan }) %>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="waitlist-section" id="waitlist">
  <div class="shell waitlist waitlist-compact">
    <div class="waitlist-copy">
      <p class="kicker">Early access</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Put the reminders in the void.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">Leave an email and we will send one note when the preview opens.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="waitlist-action">
      <%- include('partials/waitlist') %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
